> A few naming questions...
>
> >   t - an uncursed amulet of reflection named qu:12,ca:28,VS:51,wE:
> > 50,wT:41 (being worn)
>
> ? I'm totally lost on this one.

It's shorthand for where various things in the dungeon are.  The quest
portal was on level 12 (qu:12), the castle was on level 28 (ca:28),
the Vibrating Square was level 51 (VS:51).  The portal into Rodney's
tower was on level 50 (wE:50).  Rodney himself was on level 41 (wT:
41).

> >   w - a blessed +4 Hawaiian shirt named 60-cdi-hum-tou-fem-neu
>
> ? A tribute to the bones you got it from?

Yup.  That shirt came off my previous character (my 60th game on NAO).

> >   k - an uncursed lizard corpse named Ilsa-de-Seca
>
> ? No clue on this one either.

I name my lizard corpses.  I'm less likely to eat it on accident if
I've given it a name.
Ilsa-de-Seca is a character from an anime I enjoyed greatly.

> >   F - a blessed brass lantern named ASTRAL! (lit)
>
> ? You were saving the fuel for astral and named it to avoid wasting it
> early?

Yes, I was short on light sources, so I named one.  For example, if
I'm short on wands of digging, I'll name 1 EARTH! as a reminder to
save it for the endgame.  Wands of death and teleportation only get
used in certain circumstances.  Outside "the Wand of Orcus", I rarely
name those.

Wands of wishing always get named with where I found it and how many
charges it had.

